# Assignment 3 - Password Strength Checker

## Description
This script asks the user to enter a password (input is hidden while typing) and checks whether it meets five rules: at least 8 characters, an uppercase letter, a lowercase letter, a digit, and a special character. It then prints a report showing OK/Missing for each rule, plus an overall strength rating (Weak / Medium / Strong).

## File
- password_check.sh

## How to Run
chmod +x password_check.sh
./password_check.sh

## Explanation / Concepts Used
- Hidden input: read -s -p "Enter password: " reads the password without echoing it to the screen.
- String length: ${#password} gives the number of characters, used to check the minimum length of 8.
- Pattern matching (regex): Bash's [[ "$password" =~ PATTERN ]] is used to detect uppercase ([A-Z]), lowercase ([a-z]), digits ([0-9]), and special characters ([^a-zA-Z0-9]).
- Conditions: Each check uses an if statement to set a result (OK/Missing) and increase a score counter.
- Overall rating: 5/5 gives Strong, 3-4/5 gives Medium, 0-2/5 gives Weak.

## Example
Enter password:

Password Strength Report

Length          : OK
Uppercase       : OK
Lowercase       : OK
Digit           : Missing
Special Char    : OK

Overall: Medium
